"capture.prompt.shots" = "Use the blurt skill to process this batch of captures: %@\nIt is a shots session (mode: shots, no video). Each line of shots.jsonl is one capture and anchors one item: \"type\": \"shot\" is a screenshot (its primary frame; .marked.png files already carry the user’s ink; a .wav is a voice note on it — transcribe it first), \"type\": \"voice\" is a voice note with no image (\"said\" is its transcript when it is already there, else transcribe the wav).\nThis is an unattended background run started by the Blurt app: don’t ask questions and don’t start the review page; write items.json, then summarise in 2–3 sentences.";
